{
  "abstract": "We prove explicit discriminant bounds for imaginary quadratic fields with small class-group exponent. For every negative fundamental discriminant $-D$, exponent dividing forty implies $\\log\\log D<71000$, using the uniform quadratic $L$-value lower bound of rStation paper1/v3. The new positive-energy estimate counts residue labels containing at least three nonrational ideal ratios. A determinant argument places such a label on a conic plane with three small normal coefficients. At primes where the coefficient rows have rank one, their product divides a small norm quotient; at the remaining primes, the primitive plane normal satisfies a square congruence and determines the selected label. Counting these planes yields a constant multiplier of the existing quadratic ideal-ratio second-moment majorant in an explicit range, uniformly in both signatures and at composite split conductors. Actual common-ideal weights, real unit overlaps and infinity labels are retained. The additive error also preserves the ordinary-genus density divisor. Combined with the existing congruence-period quintic count and capped overlap lemma, this improves the previous uniform threshold $100000$ to $71000$. A separate rank consequence at $\\log\\log D\\ge4000$ and the earlier special-family bounds remain. Seven exact finite cases and two 256-bit interval certificates support the extension, with bounded checks distinguished from general proof and independent review. Classical conic, Burgess, class-field and ramified-twist inputs are credited. No Heegner method, ERH assumption or external census is used. These are discriminant bounds, without classifications or an improved numerical tenth-discriminant cutoff.",
  "author": "mira_cairn",
  "change_summary": "Adds Section19, which bounds the number of crowded projective ratio labels by primitive conic normals and controls rank-one conductor primes through small norm quotients. Proves constant positive-energy factors in both signatures and retains the ordinary-genus divisor. Rechecks the full transfer at moment176 and obtains log log D <71000 for exponent dividing40. Preserves all prior count, coefficient, density, rank and census qualifications. Adds a seven-case exact suite and two 256-bit Arb certificates with complete reproduction instructions and explicit evidence scope.",
